UID:41976-1777314600-1777318200@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:15 Ways to Garden Large in Small Spaces\, Palmerston Library
DESCRIPTION:Everyone with a smaller urban garden will benefit from these fun and practical ideas to expand your garden’s visual impact and intensify your garden’s yield. Includes tips on creating drama\, adding colour\, growing vertical\, the smart use of containers\, and adding multi-season plants to give your small garden greater appeal.
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/garden-wise-organic-and-sustainable-methods-15-ways-to-garden-large-in-small-spaces-palmerston-library/
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library – Palmerston\, 560 Palmerston\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6G 2P7\, Canada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Master Gardeners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T150000
DTSTAMP:20260427T235829
CREATED:20260320T205452Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260401T004533Z
UID:41893-1777471200-1777474800@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:Demo: From Balconies to Backyards: Planning a Successful Vegetable Garden\, Malvern Library
DESCRIPTION:Want to enjoy vegetables you’ve grown yourself in your own backyard or on your balcony? A Toronto Master Gardener will lead a demonstration and show how to get started to grow your own vegetables. Get some tips and learn techniques for successful growing. At the end of the program\, vegetable seeds or seedlings will be shared with attendees\, while supplies last.
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/demo-from-balconies-to-backyards-planning-a-successful-vegetable-garden-malvern-library/
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library – Malvern
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Master Gardeners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T140000
DTSTAMP:20260427T235829
CREATED:20260320T212230Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260401T004459Z
UID:41909-1777554000-1777557600@www.torontomastergardeners.ca
SUMMARY:Demo: Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spaces\, Lillian H. Smith Library
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing season\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies? This demonstration will start with how to choose soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize their positive impact on the environment. At the end of the demonstration\, materials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last.
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/demo-supporting-our-local-pollinators-in-small-spaces-lillian-h-smith-library/
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library – Lillian H. Smith\, 239 College Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, \, TorontM5T 1R5\, Canada
END:VEVENT
